From 159646dd1ab1a21951a048313a22644f5722f448 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:27:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PM P1: PM1 registers, SCI, S5 (PM_PLAN P1)

The G5 PM block stops reading zero at everything except the
Timer: PM1_STS becomes a W1C latch over the RW1C mask
(0x8501), PM1_EN stores, PM1_CNT stores SCI_EN/BM_RLD and
decodes SLP_TYP/SLP_EN, all through the existing byte-stream
assembler so byte and word accesses compose like the Timer's.
pm_advance now latches TMR_STS on the real 24-bit wrap and is
also driven from devices_tick (pm_tick), so the event latches
even if nobody reads the Timer. SCI is a level on IRQ9, gated
by SCI_EN and (sts & en), through pic_set_irq like the rest
of the fleet. S5 (SLP_TYP=7, the Q35/PIIX4 encoding P2's
DSDT must publish) logs and stops the run via stop_requested
-- an ACPI power-off finally works; other sleep types log
until P3 instead of being faked.

Timer behaviour is byte-identical: the pre-P1 "only TMR has
state" vector passes unmodified (its CNT write of 0 is a
no-op store). Vectors (tests/test_pm.c, 3 new groups):
register storage word+byte; the overflow latch, W1C
selectivity, and the SCI level following SCI_EN; the S5
decode stopping the run while type 0 does not. NC: pm.c/pm.h
reverted to the P0 version -- the P1 groups abort at the
first EN-store assert (the vectors use only pre-P1 symbols,
so the revert compiles and fails behaviourally). Gates:
make test + test-sanitize green, ISO lane green. Docs:
PM_PLAN.md (P1 receipts, D1/D2 resolved), STATUS.md,
CHANGELOG.md.
